cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use the Gerbil Atlas Explorer or its derived data, please cite the atlas
  itself (preferred-citation below) and this software.
title: Gerbil Atlas Explorer
type: software
version: 0.9.0
date-released: "2026-09-02"
repository-code: https://github.com/dstolz/GerbilAtlasExplorer
url: https://dstolz.github.io/GerbilAtlasExplorer/
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A searchable, clickable version of the Radtke-Schuller et al. (2016) Mongolian
  gerbil brain atlas: 723 structures across 62 coronal plates with stereotaxic
  coordinates, printed-label positions, regional outlines cut from the atlas's
  own drawings, a brain outline, an experimental track planner, and 3-D views.
  Derived data are released under CC BY 4.0 (see LICENSE-DATA.md).
authors:
  - family-names: Stolzberg
    given-names: Daniel
    affiliation: Caras Lab, Department of Biology, University of Maryland
keywords:
  - brain atlas
  - Mongolian gerbil
  - Meriones unguiculatus
  - stereotaxic coordinates
  - neuroscience
preferred-citation:
  type: article
  title: >-
    Brain atlas of the Mongolian gerbil (Meriones unguiculatus) in CT/MRI-aided
    stereotaxic coordinates
  authors:
    - family-names: Radtke-Schuller
      given-names: Susanne
    - family-names: Schuller
      given-names: Gerd
    - family-names: Angenstein
      given-names: Frank
    - family-names: Grosser
      given-names: Oliver S.
    - family-names: Goldschmidt
      given-names: Jürgen
    - family-names: Budinger
      given-names: Eike
  journal: Brain Structure and Function
  volume: 221
  issue: Suppl 1
  start: 1
  end: 272
  year: 2016
  doi: 10.1007/s00429-016-1259-0
